  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 1202 AM MST Sun Nov 15 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge axis will shift east of NM Monday night,  \ngiving way to increasing southwest flow aloft and moisture \nadvection Tuesday in advance of an approaching upper level trough.\nThe upper level trough is still forecast to weaken and lift\nnortheast across the region Tuesday night into Wednesday, bringing\nanother round of precipitation that will favor the northern\nmountains and areas along/west of the Continental Divide. Snow\nlevels and impacts will be similar to yesterday's event, with \npotential for a Winter Weather Advisory for the Tusas Mountains.\nthe latest model consensus on the end of the week system keeps the\ntrack mostly north of us across the southern Rockies, with a \nquick round of precipitation favoring northwest NM. However,\nforecast confidence is still low for Fri/Sat given some continued\nmodel spread. The current consensus track of the upper low/trough\nwould bring some wind impacts to our area on Friday, with some\npotential for advisory-type speeds.",
